	<key>readme</key>
	<string>Toggle the macOS system appearance.

  dark          switch to the other appearance
  dark light    force light
  dark dark     force dark

Setting the OS appearance is all this does. nvim, Alacritty, tmux and
any attached SSH devbox already follow the OS switch through the
appearance-daemon LaunchAgent (dark-notify) and tmux-dark-notify, so
there is nothing extra to drive from here. If that daemon is not
loaded, apply.sh falls back to running theme-sync directly.

Source of truth: ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/dotfiles/config/AlfredApp/dark-mode (this directory
is a symlink into it).

Replaces 'Dark Mode' by Sindre Sorhus (2017), which shipped 2.5 MB of
unused node_modules to run four lines of AppleScript.</string>
